---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import SiteLink from '../components/SiteLink.astro';
import { APP_NAME, BUSINESS_NAME, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../utils/env';

const effectiveDateISO = '2026-08-29';
const effectiveDateLabel = 'August 29, 2026';
---

<Doc
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${APP_NAME} handles data.`}
>
  <header class="doc__header">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      When analytics is on, the app sends the following to an outside
      analytics service:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        A random ID for your copy of the app. It stays the same until you
        reset your data or delete the app. It is not your name, your
        account, or your device ID.
      </li>
      <li>Which features you use, which packs you pick, and what you buy.</li>
      <li>Crash and performance reports.</li>
      <li>
        Your app version, device type, screen size, language, region, and
        time zone.
      </li>
      <li>How often you play and how long you play.</li>
      <li>
        Which accessibility settings you have turned on, such as Reduce
        Motion or Bold Text.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We use this to see which features people use, find bugs, and make the
      app better.
    </p>
    <p>
      The service has to protect this data at least as well as this policy
      and Apple require.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can turn analytics off in the app under Settings, then Privacy.
      That stops new data from being sent. It does not delete data that was
      already sent. The service does not promise a date when it deletes old
      records.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Content reports</h2>
    <p>If you send us a content report, we receive:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The email address you send it from.</li>
      <li>The reason you write.</li>
      <li>The round ID, the app version, and the build number.</li>
      <li>The drawing, but only if you choose to attach it.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We use reports to look into the problem and decide what to do. We keep
      a report only as long as we need it for that. To have your report
      deleted, email <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink> from the address you sent it from.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Tracking</h2>
    <p>
      We do not track what you do in other companies' apps or on their
      websites. Neither does our analytics service.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If we make important changes to this policy, we will post them on this
      page and update the date below.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} is published by {BUSINESS_NAME}. Email <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink> with privacy questions.
    </p>
  </section>

  <footer class="doc__meta">Effective <time datetime={effectiveDateISO}>{effectiveDateLabel}</time></footer>
</Doc>
